  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from, and <bugs> is where the App Store page sends a report. Without them a user of the release has no way back to the project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "lists/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Validator/CommonPasswordsValidator.php:31 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks it and the app fails in the code that reads it, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += lists ships it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^24.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.json, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), REUSE (REUSE.toml).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.json: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "2 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/dialogs, @nextcloud/browserslist-config.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 300 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-only.txt, AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, Apache-2.0.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, GPL-3.0-or-later.txt, ISC.txt, MIT.txt, MPL-2.0.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 33 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead."
      ]
    },
